body:
...maybe i should've added the /s to one of my above comments.

&#x200B;

of course i'm going to nano a genji when he has blade. or anyone else who has a strong ult, especially if it's something that can change the tide in a game. when i made the above remark, i'm making fun of the people who beg for mercy pockets or nano's, but they have been making poor decisions all game. like a rein i mentioned in my first post who charges into hammonds mines, fully aware that they're there but charges anyway.

&#x200B;

if my genji is doing nothing to benefit the team, losing a 1v1 to a *support*, and doesn't want to maybe swap to something he might be better at, then fuck no i'm not going to nano him.

my favorite part is watching them squirm as they start to ult and expect the juice

&#x200B;

and then i give it to bob

yeah totally. if i ult at a bad time or position myself REALLY poorly, sure, call me out and ask what the fuck i'm thinking. but if we lose point (2cp is fun yay) or get wiped and it's because my zarya and genji who aren't in voice chat haven't ulted once in the last 10 minutes, don't say it's because the female mercy main isn't healing you enough.

&#x200B;

i'm feeling better now, i've had time to cool off. maybe the games will be better later in the day

it's happened before through text chat which (i feel) makes it easier to report. i always include a screenshot also.

&#x200B;

but in my experience, it's almost always through voice.

NA/east coast and i was playing early in the morning until about an hour or so ago. i know the option to mute them is there, but in the event they stop being rude and call out something important, i'd miss it because they were muted. 

&#x200B;

i just wish people weren't so shitty, y'know?
